ion the regional escalation if  you like as well  because lebanon is entangled hezbollah  of course being  an ally of of iran but for the time  being it seems  that hezbollah is keen on not opening a  front  and hezbollah telling the israelis this  is in response to israeli um  airstrikes and the ball is now in your  court  zaina just tell me about the areas where  this is happening on the border is it  i mean are there population centers  there a lot of the pictures we're  looking at right now seem to be sort of  a lot of  uh empty land but you can tell us more  about the geography  yes empty land both of them have been  very careful both the israelis and  hezbollah to avoid any casualties  first of all shibash the shiva forms um  these this this area is considered by  lebanon as occupied  uh territory um the israelis see this as  part of the golan heights the united  nations is still not  determined because syria has not given  uh maps to prove that this is lebanon  lebanese territory but the bottom line  is for hezbollah to choose  to target shabbat farms an area that  lebanon considers occupied territory  it too is trying not to escalate  the situation it didn't decide to target  for example  israeli population centers along the  border  and even the israeli airstrike early on  thursday  um did not target um hezbollah positions  they said  near hezbollah position so both sides  really treading carefully because  um any any wrong move here uh could  lead to all-out war and we've we've said  this time and time again over the past  few months  when uh there has been cross-border fire  each side  is not in a position now to deal with an  all-out war especially lebanon for  example  a very a precarious situation the  economy has  all but collapsed if hezbollah does  ignite a war  it already has very few friends in this  country if you like blaming it for  for controlling the decision on whether  to launch war  or or peace in in lebanon so right now  the indication  i